ample a  very large jointed Naval drills  happening off the east coast of the  Korean Peninsula involving the Ronald  Ronald Reagan at one of uh the United  States Nimitz class aircraft carriers  it's the first large exercises taking  place like that since 2017. and Rob has  there been any reaction from North Korea  to Harris's visit  you know just as we as we see a military  cooperation picking up we're also seeing  a return to an awful lot of the rhetoric  and the uh the the combative language  from North Korea and also a lot of its  testing and in fact  um we are expecting according to South  Korean intelligence officials that the  north has completed preparations for  another nuclear test now they haven't  done a nuclear test since 2017 as well  so you do get this sense of things  slipping back in time just Wednesday  evening we have the launch of two more  short-range ballistic missiles there was  another on Sunday there has been a  continuous missile testing really since  the start of this year and it was only a  few weeks ago that the North Korean  leader Kim Jong-un  announced that North Korea had arrived  as a nuclear-armed power it's now  enshrined in law and it's worth bearing  in mind that the last major U.S  leadership visit to the DMZ was 2019  that was a president Donald Trump when  he famously walked between the blue Huts  shook hands with Kim Jong-un stepped  across into North Korea at the height of  all of that Summit diplomacy with hopes  that we were about to see some  breakthrough and having the north agree  to denuclearize I think this visit back  to the usual sort of going up to the DMZ  meeting  the U.S personnel there and staring  across into North Korea that you'd never  actually we are not meeting with at the  moment I think that kind of shows you  where the relations have slipped to at  the moment indeed all right we  appreciate you breaking all down for us  Rob McBride laborers in South Korea
 

